{
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "autoloader-generic",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "The app ships no composer/autoload.php, so the server registers its generic loader for lib/ and looks every class up in the file system.",
        "  A composer/composer.json with config.vendor-dir \".\", config.optimize-autoloader true, a config.autoloader-suffix and autoload.psr-4 {\"OCA\\\\LeiterrundeSchulungen\\\\\": \"../lib/\"} makes composer dump-autoload write composer/autoload.php with a class map; the code of the app does not change."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ocp-since-above-min",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "lib/AppInfo/Application.php:37 OCP\\App\\IAppManager::isEnabledForAnyone(): there since Nextcloud 32, the app declares from 29",
        "lib/Controller/PageController.php:37 OCP\\App\\IAppManager::isEnabledForAnyone(): there since Nextcloud 32, the app declares from 29"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "2 uses in 2 files of the public API that the oldest majors of Nextcloud 29 to 36 do not have yet. Either min-version in appinfo/info.xml goes up, or the app does without it there.",
        "  lib/AppInfo/Application.php:37 OCP\\App\\IAppManager::isEnabledForAnyone(): there since Nextcloud 32, the app declares from 29",
        "  lib/Controller/PageController.php:37 OCP\\App\\IAppManager::isEnabledForAnyone(): there since Nextcloud 32, the app declares from 29"
      ]
    },
