    {
      "id": "migration-bool-notnull",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "lib/Migration/Version1000Date20261105000000.php:28 lr_training_types.counts_hours, in Nextcloud 29 to 32",
        "lib/Migration/Version1000Date20261105000000.php:29 lr_training_types.required, in Nextcloud 29 to 32",
        "lib/Migration/Version1000Date20261105000000.php:30 lr_training_types.required_for_event, in Nextcloud 29 to 32",
        "lib/Migration/Version1000Date20261105000000.php:32 lr_training_types.active, in Nextcloud 29 to 32"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "4 boolean columns are NotNull. Oracle cannot store false in such a column, so the server stops the migration with an exception. A boolean column needs notnull false.",
        "  Up to Nextcloud 32 the server checks this only where info.xml lists no database, or lists oci among them. From Nextcloud 33 on the server makes the column nullable on Oracle itself.",
        "  lib/Migration/Version1000Date20261105000000.php:28 lr_training_types.counts_hours, in Nextcloud 29 to 32",
        "  lib/Migration/Version1000Date20261105000000.php:29 lr_training_types.required, in Nextcloud 29 to 32",
        "  lib/Migration/Version1000Date20261105000000.php:30 lr_training_types.required_for_event, in Nextcloud 29 to 32",
        "  lib/Migration/Version1000Date20261105000000.php:32 lr_training_types.active, in Nextcloud 29 to 32"
      ],
      "folds": [
        {
          "at": 5,
          "count": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "transaction-manual",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [
        "lib/Service/TrainingSessionService.php:68"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "1 transaction is opened and closed by hand. The trait TTransactional has atomic() since Nextcloud 24 and atomicRetry() since Nextcloud 27, which repeats a transaction that ran into a deadlock, as the manual recommends.",
        "  lib/Service/TrainingSessionService.php:68"
      ]
    },
